PRIVACY POLICY FOR PDF MASTER
Last Updated: March 15, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how PDF Master ("we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, and discloses information about you when you use our mobile application on iOS. PDF Master is a premium productivity tool for merging, scanning, and converting documents.

1. Information We Collect
To provide the core features of the App (PDF merging, document scanning, and file conversion), we collect limited data. Your privacy is our priority, and all document processing happens directly on your device.

a. Files and Documents

Purpose: To perform functions like merging multiple PDFs, converting images to PDF, or scanning documents.

Processing: All file manipulations (merging, converting, and editing) are performed locally on your device. We do not upload your personal documents, scans, or private files to our servers.

b. Camera Access

Purpose: The App requires access to your device’s camera to enable the "Scan" feature.

Processing: The camera is used solely to capture images of documents. These images are processed locally to create PDF files and are not transmitted to us.

c. Usage Data & Diagnostics

Purpose: To improve App stability and performance, we may collect anonymous crash reports and performance data.

Processing: This data is aggregated and not linked to your personal identity.

2. In-App Purchases (IAP) and Payments
PDF Master offers premium features through In-App Purchases.

Payment Processing: All payments are processed through Apple’s App Store. We do not collect or store your credit card numbers, bank account information, or any other financial data.

Transaction Information: When you make a purchase, Apple provides us with a digital receipt to confirm your subscription or lifetime access. This information is used solely to unlock the premium features of the App.

Privacy: For more information on how Apple handles your payment data, please review the Apple Privacy Policy.

3. Data Sharing and Disclosure
We do not sell your personal data or your documents to third parties. We do not use third-party advertising or tracking SDKs in this App. Your usage habits and files remain private.

4. Security
We take reasonable measures to protect your information. Because PDF Master functions offline for document processing, your sensitive files stay on your device and are not stored on our infrastructure.

5. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. If we make changes, we will notify you by revising the date at the top of the policy.

